  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Colleges and employers pay attention to students who plan, communicate and finish. They judge you by habits shown over time.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is a written weekly plan.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and college and career readiness skills: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools draft, summarise and suggest options. Routine output becomes common quickly.
  </p>
  <p>
    Judgment, accountability and trust hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI for drafts and practice; later, own the decisions and the relationships.
  </p>

